  "user_request_original": "Optimize a fixed 16-layer alternating ZnSe/ZnS multilayer stack on Ge substrate at normal incidence. Initialize with thicknesses [1130, 874, 481, 227, 411, 966, 878, 1273, 500, 465, 454, 403, 275, 938, 733, 1257] nm. Freeze layers 4-11 (indices 4 through 11 inclusive) at their current values. Optimize only layers 0, 1, 2, 3, 12, 13, 14, 15 with bounds ±40 nm from initialization. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer. Evaluate mean transmittance in 8000-11000 nm band (maximize) and 3000-5000 nm band (minimize) with equal weighting. Total layer count: 16 finite layers. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 8000-11000 nm, 3000-5000 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 8000-11000 nm band; Low transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: High transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count not exceeding 16.",
